<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Kennedy called this morning and was seen the same day. Yesterday afternoon he developed chills, aching muscles, a sore throat and a dry cough, and last night his temperature at home was 38.9 °C. Following his written sick-day rules, he doubled his hydrocortisone this morning, taking 20 mg on waking, and has 10 mg ready for noon and 10 mg for 4 pm. He has drunk plenty, with salty broth. He has not vomited or had diarrhea and has kept every tablet down. He feels weak and tired but has had no lightheadedness on standing, fainting, confusion, or abdominal pain. Several colleagues have had influenza this week. He had this season&apos;s influenza vaccine at his first visit five weeks ago. He has his emergency injection kit with him. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Yesterday afternoon</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>About one day</td></tr><tr><td>Character</td><td>Fever, chills, myalgia, sore throat, dry cough</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Moderate; highest temperature 38.9 °C</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Influenza among colleagues; vaccinated this season; primary adrenal insufficiency on replacement</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Hydrocortisone doubled this morning under his sick-day rules; fluids with salt</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>Weakness; no vomiting, diarrhea, lightheadedness, confusion, or abdominal pain</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

